y inositol phosphates&#x02013;a possible mechanism. <source>FEBS Lett.</source> <volume>263</volume>:<fpage>5</fpage>&#x02013;9.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2185036</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal">Ishiai, M., M. Kurosaki, R. Pappu, K. Okawa, I. Ronko, C. Fu, M. Shibata, A. Iwamatsu, A.C. Chan, and T. Kurosaki. <year>1999</year>. BLNK required for coupling Syk to PLC gamma 2 and Rac1-JNK in B cells. <source>Immunity.</source> <volume>10</volume>:<fpage>117</fpage>&#x02013;125.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10023776</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal">Jaconi, M.E., D.P. Lew, A. Monod, and K.H. Krause. <year>1993</year>. The regulation of store-dependent Ca2&#x0002b; influx in HL-60 granulocytes involves GTP-sensitive elements. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>268</volume>:<fpage>26075</fpage>&#x02013;26078.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8253721</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Kiselyov, K., D.M. Shin, N. Shcheynikov, T. Kurosaki, and S. Muallem. <year>2001</year>. Regulation of Ca2&#x0002b;-release-activated Ca2&#x0002b; current (Icrac) by ryanodine receptors in inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate-receptor-deficient DT40 cells. <source>Biochem. J.</source> <volume>360</volume>:<fpage>17</fpage>&#x02013;22.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11695987</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Kurosaki, T. <year>2000</year>. Functional dissection of BCR signaling pathways. <source>Curr. Opin. Immunol.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>276</fpage>&#x02013;281.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10781408</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Lee, K.M., K. Toscas, and M.L. Villereal. <year>1993</year>. Inhibition of bradykinin- and thapsigargin-induced Ca2&#x0002b; entry by tyrosine kinase inhibitors. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>268</volume>:<fpage>9945</fpage>&#x02013;9948.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7683685</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Lewis, R.S. <year>1999</year>. Store-operated calcium channels. <source>Adv. Second Messenger Phosphoprotein Res.</source> <volume>33</volume>:<fpage>279</fpage>&#x02013;307.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10218123</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Lewis, R.S., and M.D. Cahalan. <year>1989</year>. Mitogen-induced oscillations of cytosolic Ca2&#x0002b; and transmembrane Ca2&#x0002b; current in human leukemic T cells. <source>Cell Regul.</source> <volume>1</volume>:<fpage>99</fpage>&#x02013;112.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2519622</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Liou, J., M.L. Kim, W.D. Heo, J.T. Jones, J.W. Myers, J.E. Ferrell Jr., and T. Meyer. <year>2005</year>. STIM is a Ca2&#x0002b; sensor essential for Ca2&#x0002b;-store-depletion-triggered Ca2&#x0002b; influx. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>15</volume>:<fpage>1235</fpage>&#x02013;1241.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16005298</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Liu, K.Q., S.C. Bunnell, C.B. Gurniak, and L.J. Berg. <year>1998</year>. T cell receptor-initiated calcium release is uncoupled from capacitative calcium entry in Itk-deficient T cells. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>187</volume>:<fpage>1721</fpage>&#x02013;1727.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9584150</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Luckhoff, A., and D.E. Clapham. <year>1992</year>. Inositol 1,3,4,5-tetrakisphosphate activates an endothelial Ca(2&#x0002b;)- permeable channel. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>355</volume>:<fpage>356</fpage>&#x02013;358.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1309941</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Luik, R.M., M.M. Wu, J. Buchanan, and R.S. Lewis. <year>2006</year>. The elementary unit of store-operated Ca2&#x0002b; entry: local activation of CRAC channels by STIM1 at ER-plasma membrane junctions. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>174</volume>:<fpage>815</fpage>&#x02013;825.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16966423</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Ma, H.T., K. Venkatachalam, H.S. Li, C. Montell, T. Kurosaki, R.L. Patterson, and D.L. Gill. <year>2001</year>. Assessment of the role of the inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate receptor in the activation of transient receptor potential channels and store-operated Ca2&#x0002b; entry channels. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>276</volume>:<fpage>18888</fpage>&#x02013;18896.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11259416</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">McDonald, T.V., B.A. Premack, and P. Gardner. <year>1993</year>. Flash photolysis of caged inositol 1,4,5-trisphosphate activates plasma membrane calcium current in human T cells. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>268</volume>:<fpage>3889</fpage>&#x02013;3896.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8382682</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Mizuguchi, J., Y. Yamanashi, K. Ehara, T. Tamura, H. Nariuchi, Y. Gyotoku, H. Fukazawa, Y. Uehara, and T. Yamamoto. <year>1992</year>. Tyrosine protein kinase is involved in anti-IgM-mediated signaling in BAL17 B lymphoma cells. <source>J. Immunol.</source> <volume>148</volume>:<fpage>689</fpage>&#x02013;694.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1730866</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Mori, Y., M. Wakamori, T. Miyakawa, M. Hermosura, Y. Hara, M. Nishida, K. Hirose, A. Mizushima, M. Kurosaki, E. Mori, et al. <year>2002</year>. Transient receptor potential 1 regulates capacitative Ca(2&#x0002b;) entry and Ca(2&#x0002b;) release from endoplasmic reticulum in B lymphocytes. <source>J. Exp. Med.</source> <volume>195</volume>:<fpage>673</fpage>&#x02013;681.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11901194</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Nagao, Y., M. Noji, Y. Asano, T. Hamano, and M. Nakanishi. <year>1996</year>. Calcium signals in helper T cells after interaction with antigen- specific and antigen-nonspecific B cells. <source>Biol. Pharm. Bull.</source> <volume>19</volume>:<fpage>697</fpage>&#x02013;700.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8741577</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Onoda, T., H. Iinuma, Y. Sasaki, M. Hamada, K. Isshiki, H. Naganawa, T. Takeuchi, K. Tatsuta, and K. Umezawa. <year>1989</year>. Isolation of a novel tyrosine kinase inhibitor, lavendustin A, from <italic>Streptomyces griseolavendus.</italic> <source>J. Nat. Prod.</source> <volume>52</volume>:<fpage>1252</fpage>&#x02013;1257.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2614420</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Parekh, A.B., and R. Penner. <year>1995</year>. Depletion-activated calcium current is inhibited by protein kinase in RBL-2H3 cells. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>92</volume>:<fpage>7907</fpage>&#x02013;7911.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7644512</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Parekh, A.B., and R. Penner. <year>1997</year>. Store depletion and calcium influx. <source>Physiol. Rev.</source> <volume>77</volume>:<fpage>901</fpage>&#x02013;930.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9354808</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Patterson, R.L., D.B. van Rossum, and D.L. Gill. <year>1999</year>. Store-operated Ca2&#x0002b; entry: evidence for a secretion-like coupling model. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>98</volume>:<fpage>487</fpage>&#x02013;499.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10481913</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Peinelt, C., M. Vig, D.L. Koomoa, A. Beck, M.J. Nadler, M. Koblan-Huberson, A. Lis, A. Fleig, R. Penner, and J.P. Kinet. <year>2006</year>. Amplification of CRAC current by STIM1 and CRACM1 (Orai1). <source>Nat. Cell Bio